# Generated Artifacts

## Source of Truth

- Do not manually edit generated bindings, headers, or generated artifacts
  unless the generation source itself is being changed and regeneration is part
  of the task.
- Update the generator input, schema, Rust export, build script, or binding
  source first; then regenerate the derived artifact.
- Keep generated Dart bindings, cbindgen headers, exported symbols, and Rust FFI
  signatures aligned.
- Review generated diffs for ABI, layout, naming, and nullability changes before
  accepting them.

## Suppressions

- Generated files may use broader lint suppressions only when allowed by
  `error_handling.mdc`.
- Do not copy generated-file suppressions into handwritten code.

## Build Outputs

- Do not treat `build/`, `target/`, coverage output, temporary generated files,
  or ad-hoc binaries as source files.
- Do not commit regenerated build outputs unless the repository intentionally
  tracks that artifact.
